      <Docs>
        <summary>
          <para>Use a specific scene mode.</para>
          <para>Enabling this disables control.aeMode, control.awbMode and control.afMode controls; the camera device will ignore those settings while USE_SCENE_MODE is active (except for FACE_PRIORITY scene mode). Other control entries are still active. This setting can only be used if scene mode is supported (i.e. android.control.availableSceneModes contain some modes other than DISABLED).</para>
          <para>For extended scene modes such as BOKEH, please use USE_EXTENDED_SCENE_MODE instead.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/hardware/camera2/CameraMetadata#CONTROL_MODE_USE_SCENE_MODE" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.hardware.camera2.CameraMetadata.CONTROL_MODE_USE_SCENE_MODE</code>.</a></format></para>
